A mutex whose oldest waiter comes to lend stays at the back of its holder's ring.
The first mutex no longer says whether any lends, and the holder may miss its lender.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a mutex whose waiters lend comes after one whose waiters do not

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -615,7 +615,7 @@ static void mutex_waiters_changed(struct mutex *m, bool was)
     bool lends = mutex_lends(m);
     if (lends != was) {
         held_remove(h, m);
-        held_push(h, m, lends);
+        held_push(h, m, false);
     }
     thread_settle(h);
 }
